OL,3,GNEWSAAlan Carr lodges plans to turn
OL,4,Acastle potting shed into cafe
OL,5,
OL,6,FComedian Alan Carr has lodged plans to
OL,7,Fconvert a potting shed at his castle in
OL,8,Fthe Scottish Borders into a cafe and
OL,9,Festate shop.
OL,11,FThe Celebrity Traitors winner bought
OL,12,F19th Century Ayton Castle earlier this
OL,13,Fyear.
OL,15,FA new TV series is planned following
OL,16,Fhis attempt to turn the ageing estate
OL,17,Finto a workable home.
OL,19,FNow he has put in a planning
OL,20,Fapplication to Scottish Borders Council
OL,21,F(SBC) to redevelop a part of the
OL,22,Festate.
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
